location.method:
The point is the area centroid of the Project Clydesdale PUD-871 tract, computed from its official metes-and-bounds description. That description appears in the TMAPC minutes of 2025-06-04 (Meeting No. 2938, PUD-871 Property Description, p.23-24). The tract is part of Section 27, T21N, R13E, Indian Meridian, Tulsa County. The description lists 18 calls starting at the W1/4 corner (NW corner of the SW4) of Section 27, then applies 'LESS and EXCEPT ... the East 85.00 feet', stated as 496.1591 acres.

The Point of Beginning comes from the federal BLM CadNSDI PLSS layer: the Section 27 polygon (FRSTDIVID OK170210N0130E0SN270), vertex (-95.91989002, 36.27131588). This is captured as blm-plss-ok-t21n-r13e-sec27, sha256 b1d3629bd818cc2882d3b0da502a9644dba6fcb4e776ad046f9fb4165ea755e8.

Calls were traversed in US survey feet. Grid bearings were rotated to true by the Lambert grid convergence of +1.2276 deg (n=0.590147, lon0=-98).

The local planar result was converted to degrees with GRS80/WGS84 meridian and prime-vertical radii. The script is /Users/kian/.claude/jobs/ca498c66/tmp/blind/16/pud871_centroid.py.

Validation:
- traverse closure 0.00 m;
- 505.2 ac before the east-85-ft exception, matching the stated 'approximately 506 acres';
- 496.159 ac after it, matching the stated 496.1591 ac exactly;
- the computed E1/4 corner lies about 5 m from the BLM E1/4 corner, and the south 50-ft offset line about 2 m from BLM.

An independent consistency check is the BOCC minutes of 2026-03-16. They place the PROJECT CLYDESDALE plat '0.3 mi. E. and 0.5 mi. N. of the E. 76th N. and N. Whirlpool Drive junction', which is consistent with this latitude.

